@page
@model GovBidPro.Web.Pages.DataPolicyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Data policy";
}
<h1>Prohibited data notice</h1>
<p>GovBid Pro Release 1 is a commercial service for government contractors. It is <strong>not</strong> an approved environment for regulated government information.</p>
<h2>Do not upload or enter</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Classified information</strong> of any level. It must never be entered into GovBid Pro.</li>
    <li><strong>Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI)</strong>, including anything marked CUI or with legacy markings such as FOUO.</li>
    <li><strong>Federal Contract Information (FCI)</strong> that your contract requires you to safeguard.</li>
    <li>Other records you are not legally permitted to share with a third-party service.</li>
</ul>
<h2>How this is enforced</h2>
<p>Before every upload you must classify the file and confirm it contains no prohibited content. GovBid Pro also checks uploads for common security markings and rejects files that contain them before they are stored. These checks are a safeguard, not a guarantee: they cannot prove that a file is free of FCI or CUI, and they do not replace your own obligations.</p>
<p>If you find that prohibited content was uploaded, a company administrator can quarantine the document, which immediately blocks all access to it. Then contact your security officer.</p>
<h2>Certifications and claims</h2>
<p>GovBid Pro holds no FedRAMP authorization, CMMC certification or Section 508 conformance claim. It does not determine legal compliance, verify certifications such as VetCert, or submit proposals on your behalf.</p>
<h2>Retention</h2>
<p>Deleted documents can be restored for a limited recovery period and are then purged from live storage. Copies may remain in encrypted backups until those backups expire. Retention periods are provisional and subject to legal review.</p>
